tly a byte copy of en (value === currentSource) or was previously recorded as such (previous[path] === hash(value)). A leaf holding a genuine translation satisfies neither, by the mechanism's own documented ruling (#12069 Option A: 'a leaf someone actually TRANSLATED ... gets no record and stays legacy-trusted'). Ran `pnpm i18n:extract` after writing the translations: it rewrote nothing else and added NO hash entry for this leaf — confirming the trace. So 'give the leaf a source-hash entry' (the issue's suggested shape / dispatch A2) is architecturally unreachable while the leaf holds a real translation; this is not a regression, it's the pre-existing status quo for every hand-translated objects-section leaf (measured population below).",
